#!/usr/bin/env -S uv run --quiet --script
# /// script
# requires-python = ">=3.11"
# dependencies = ["tomlkit>=0.13"]
# ///
"""omarchy-keys: generate every key binding output from bindings.toml.

Usage:
  omarchy-keys check    [--bindings F] [--settings F] [--karabiner F] [--offline]
  omarchy-keys print    [--bindings F] [--settings F] [--offline]
  omarchy-keys generate --out DIR [--bindings F] [--settings F] [--karabiner F]
                        [--offline] [--diff]
  omarchy-keys install  [--dry-run] [--only PART ...] [--bindings F] [--settings F]
                        [--karabiner F]

check     parse and validate bindings.toml (chords, duplicates, owners, every
          'wm' command against 'omniwmctl query commands', every 'hs' action
          against the Hammerspoon action list) and lint the Karabiner rules.
print     print the final binding table: chord -> owner -> action.
generate  write, into DIR (never into the live locations):
            DIR/karabiner.json
            DIR/settings.toml        live OmniWM settings + generated [[hotkeys]]
                                     + the Omarchy settings (read-only on live)
            DIR/hammerspoon/omarchy/generated/bindings.lua
            DIR/KEYBINDINGS.md
install   regenerate and deploy to the live locations (for re-runs after the
          first cutover; the Omarchy menu's "Regenerate keybindings" uses it):
            ~/.hammerspoon/omarchy/generated/bindings.lua   (atomic rename)
            ~/.config/omniwm/settings.toml  merged again from the current live
                file under the omarchy-omniwm-set lock, backup, atomic rename,
                ping + corrupt-file check
            ~/.config/karabiner/karabiner.json  (backup, atomic rename)
            ~/.config/omarchy-mac/KEYBINDINGS.md
          Backups of karabiner.json go to ~/.local/state/omarchy-mac/backups/
          (newest 5). --dry-run prints what would change and writes nothing.
          --only hammerspoon|settings|karabiner|docs (repeatable) installs just
          those parts, in the order given, so a first cutover can follow its
          own sequence. This is the safe way to deploy settings.toml: it is
          re-merged onto the live file under the lock, so values OmniWM wrote
          itself (Overview zoom, switcher scope ...) are kept.

Defaults: --bindings <script dir>/../bindings.toml,
          --settings ~/.config/omniwm/settings.toml (read only),
          --karabiner ~/.config/karabiner/karabiner.json (read only; its
          'devices' and 'virtual_hid_keyboard' sections are kept).
--offline validates 'wm' commands against 'omniwmctl help' text only and
skips the Karabiner lint if karabiner_cli is missing.

Owners: OW = OmniWM native hotkey (Carbon), HS = Hammerspoon hs.hotkey,
KB = Karabiner shell_command, KE = Karabiner key emission.
"""
